  "duration": 204.8464375,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.1,
      "text": "You've put in the time to learn the mechanics."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.8,
      "end": 6.4,
      "text": "You now know how to use AI, and you understand the engine underneath,"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.98,
      "end": 9.96,
      "text": "which means its strange behavior finally makes sense."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.84,
      "end": 12.74,
      "text": "You've achieved the core goal of this course."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.28,
      "end": 14.98,
      "text": "You are now smarter than the tool."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.86,
      "end": 20.16,
      "text": "So that brings us to the question almost everyone is arguing about right now."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.9,
      "end": 22.42,
      "text": "Where does all this actually land?"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.26,
      "end": 26.18,
      "text": "Moving from understanding how a piece of software functions"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.18,
      "end": 29.84,
      "text": "to projecting its impact on society is a massive leap."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.54,
      "end": 34.52,
      "text": "We are leaving the realm of factual certainty and entering a space of wild speculation."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.54,
      "end": 37.12,
      "text": "You've definitely heard the voices already."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.78,
      "end": 42.54,
      "text": "You probably know an AI optimist who thinks this technology is amazing, fantastic,"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.22,
      "end": 45.56,
      "text": "and worthy of every other superlative they can string together."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.24,
      "end": 50.22,
      "text": "And you know an AI warrior who is absolutely certain it's going to hurt society."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.32,
      "end": 52.14,
      "text": "Here's the honest part."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.84,
      "end": 53.76,
      "text": "Nobody knows."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.76,
      "end": 57.54,
      "text": "Not them, not us, not the people building AI."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.46,
      "end": 62.8,
      "text": "Being an expert at coding neural networks does not grant the ability to predict human history."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.46,
      "end": 66.66,
      "text": "Because technical expertise does not equal prophetic vision,"
    },
    {
      "start": 67.06,
      "end": 71.56,
      "text": "both the utopian promises and the doomsday warnings you hear are ultimately just guesses."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.6,
      "end": 73.98,
      "text": "Think back to history class."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.56,
      "end": 78.78,
      "text": "Centuries ago, map makers had to figure out what to do with vast stretches of ocean"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.78,
      "end": 80.18,
      "text": "they simply did not understand."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.18,
      "end": 86.02,
      "text": "Their solution was to fill those uncharted waters with imagined sea monsters and strange serpents."
    },
    {
      "start": 86.66,
      "end": 91.86,
      "text": "The future of AI is exactly like the unknown parts of the ocean on those old maps."
    },
    {
      "start": 92.66,
      "end": 96.52,
      "text": "The AI warriors look out at that blank space and draw modern monsters."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.18,
      "end": 101.72,
      "text": "They picture a technology that destroys jobs, hack systems, and takes over the world."
    },
    {
      "start": 102.5,
      "end": 106.16,
      "text": "Meanwhile, AI optimists stare at the exact same unknown waters"
    },
    {
      "start": 106.16,
      "end": 109.82,
      "text": "and see only easy clear sailing through open channels."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.68,
      "end": 115.42,
      "text": "Both extreme optimism and extreme dread are just the human mind drawing sea monsters"
    },
    {
      "start": 115.42,
      "end": 118.1,
      "text": "to cope with the anxiety of an empty map."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.9,
      "end": 122.68,
      "text": "But look at what those early sailors actually found when they pushed past the edge."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.2,
      "end": 126.96,
      "text": "They didn't run into sea monsters and they very rarely got easy clear sailing."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.68,
      "end": 130.52,
      "text": "What they usually encountered was something completely unexpected."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.52,
      "end": 135.1,
      "text": "Throughout this section, we are going to take both views of our map seriously."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.1,
      "end": 139.78,
      "text": "The very real risks of the monsters and the genuine benefits of the open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.5,
      "end": 142.28,
      "text": "As we do, only one thing is certain."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.92,
      "end": 144.06,
      "text": "AI is here to stay."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.84,
      "end": 149.12,
      "text": "That doesn't mean it keeps getting better forever, just that the technology isn't going away."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.86,
      "end": 153.24,
      "text": "Navigating successfully doesn't require predicting the future perfectly."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.92,
      "end": 160.5,
      "text": "It requires accepting the permanence of the technology and staying agile enough to handle the reality of whatever actually emerges."
    },
    {
      "start": 160.5,
      "end": 166.24,
      "text": "This chart outlines the framework we will use for this section, built around three guiding questions."
    },
    {
      "start": 167.02,
      "end": 170.4,
      "text": "One, why do people disagree so much about AI's future?"
    },
    {
      "start": 171.26,
      "end": 175.48,
      "text": "Two, what could AI do to make society better and where could it go wrong?"
    },
    {
      "start": 176.26,
      "end": 180.14,
      "text": "And three, how could AI change my future life and work?"
    },
    {
      "start": 181.02,
      "end": 186.68,
      "text": "Focusing on these specific inquiries arms us with a compass rather than a predetermined map."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.68,
      "end": 190.86,
      "text": "The destination ahead of us is still entirely unmapped."
    },
    {
      "start": 191.46,
      "end": 192.82,
      "text": "Nobody has a map of what's coming."
    },
    {
      "start": 193.44,
      "end": 195.38,
      "text": "You're ready to sail into the blank space."
    },
    {
      "start": 196.16,
      "end": 201.18,
      "text": "Navigating the future requires stepping into the unknown with readiness rather than fear."
    }
  ],
